Description: LinuxDroid Desktop Environment — Wayland shell for LinuxDroid
 LDDE is a production-grade, minimal, Linux-native Wayland desktop
 environment designed mobile-first for Linux running through LinuxDroid.
 .
 It provides a complete Wayland compositor shell including:
  - Application launcher with search and category filtering
  - Persistent dock with running-app indicators
  - Window manager with mobile-optimized touch interaction
  - Application switcher with MRU ordering
  - Notification center with D-Bus integration
  - System UI with status bar, quick controls, and clock
  - Centralized settings subsystem
 .
 LDDE integrates with LDDM (LinuxDroid Display Manager) and Weston
 as a Wayland client shell. It is strictly a Wayland client; it does
 not require X11, framebuffer, or Android APIs.
